["sleeptrain-1xecsu3","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","pain",["partner_disagreement","marriage_strain","parent_mental_health"],"I’m still not entirely sold on sleep training, though my husband has been urging us to consider. But the lack of sleep is starting to take a major toll on our physical and mental health, our relationship, and our ability to function day to day.","Breastfeeding mother of a 10-month-old; husband pushes sleep training."],
["sleeptrain-1xecsu3","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","pain",["only_mum_settles","feeding_to_sleep","partner_split_nights"],"I’m exhausted from being the only person who can reliably settle him overnight, and it’s becoming really difficult for my husband to take over.","Only nursing settles the night wakes."],
["sleeptrain-1xecsu3","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","pain",["daycare_naps","relative_caregiver_conflict"],"**Monday/Tuesday:** Daycare. He typically takes two naps, usually around 35–45 minutes each.","Daycare days vs grandmother days give different naps."],
["sleeptrain-1xecsu3","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","question",["sleep_training_values","information_overload"],"**We’re not looking for judgment or someone to tell us we’ve created bad habits. We’ve responded to our baby’s needs, and we don’t regret that. We’re just at a point where what we’re doing isn’t sustainable anymore","Pre-empting the usual replies."],
