["sleeptrain-1xeekg1","","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","failure_story",["ferber","cry_it_out"],"We first tried Ferber at 5 months, but my baby was NOT having it. It seemed to work for the first two days, but by day 5 he was absolutely terrified of his room and crib. We decided to stop, wait another four weeks, and try CIO instead since the check-ins seemed to make things worse.","Ferber abandoned, CIO later."],
["sleeptrain-1xeekg1","","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","pain",["short_naps","cry_it_out","contact_naps"],"I’m thrilled that his nighttime sleep has improved, but I feel like we’ve traded one sleep problem for another.","CIO fixed nights; naps fell to 30 minutes."],
["NewParents-1xef8h4","","new_mother","baby_2_4_months","pain",["maternal_exhaustion","parent_identity"],"My baby is 11 weeks old, and I love him more than life itself, but holy shit, I am EXHAUSTED. Mentally, physically, spiritually. I have about three brain cells left, and two of them are crying.","Breastfeeding mother's vent."],
